  "details": "Please note that \"4\" comes from a game-imposed hard limit on an avatar's concurrent playing audio (or so I am told). If this limiting behavior is not intentional, then this request is moot and should be discarded.\n\nCurrently, adding variation to audio, or having many sound effects, will dramatically reduce the avatar's performance rank. In my opinion, this makes little sense, considering the fact that you *can't actually play more than four sources at once in the first place.*\n\nOf course, spatialized audio is not cheap; this fact is not being contested, and the limit of 4 playing at once seems pretty sensible to me. This request instead addresses the performance rank impact of having more pooled or available than that ceiling of 4. Unlike disabled avatar objects, it's just not possible to have them all on at once no matter how hard you try. This fact makes it a bit perplexing as to why having more than this cap on an avatar would give it a worse performance rank.",
